# Cursor subagent models

When using the Task tool — including `mult`, `orchestrate`, or any subagent spawn — pass only the slugs below.

The role list applies only when the spawn runs a skill (`metadata.recommendedRole`):

- `composer-2.5-fast` for `explore` / `follow`
- `cursor-grok-4.7-medium` for `implement` / `task-owner`
- `cursor-grok-4.7-high` for `quality-gate`
- `auto` for `deterministic`
- `inherit` if the parent is already that model

When freely orchestrating, with no skill role, the default general-purpose model is `cursor-grok-4.7-medium`.

Never pass `claude-opus-5-thinking-high`, `claude-opus-5`, other `claude-*`, `gpt-5.6-*`, `gpt-5.3-codex`, `gemini-3.1-pro`, `glm-5.2-high`, `kimi-k3-max`, `cursor-grok-4.6-high`, or `cursor-grok-4.5-high`, even if Task lists them.

If the `orchestrate` SKILL.md you opened names Opus, Luna, Terra, or Sol, you opened the Claude or Codex copy. Read `${HOME}/.cursor/skills/orchestrate/SKILL.md` and follow that instead.

Do not add this rule to `AGENTS.md` (Claude/Codex must keep their own spawn tables).
